+## 1. F-12 server-side state independently re-confirmed (23:0xZ)
+
+`OPTIONS https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com/api/v1/auth/register` with any
+`Access-Control-Request-Headers` set → **400 "Disallowed CORS origin"** for a
+non-allow-listed Origin, and the failure response itself carries:
+
+```
+access-control-allow-headers: Accept, Accept-Language, Authorization,
+  Content-Language, Content-Type, Origin, Referer, X-Correlation-ID,
+  X-Forwarded-For, X-Guest-Mode, X-SupremeAI-Key
+access-control-allow-credentials: true
+access-control-max-age: 600
+```
+
+This is byte-for-byte the same 11-header list cycle-22 captured from the
+allow-listed app origin — the header gap is server-side ground truth,
+independent of origin guessing. The Studio bundle's headers absent from it:
+`X-CSRF-Token, X-Conversation-Id, X-Device-Fingerprint, X-JIT-OTP,
+X-Request-ID, X-Trusted-Browser`.
+
+## 2. NEW: the customer surface's CORS source is gateway/service/app.py:271 — NOT app_builder.py:408
+
+In-repo attribution on live main ebe630c:
+
+- `core/app_builder.py:408` (the **core API app**) allow-list **already
+  includes** `X-Device-Fingerprint, X-CSRF-Token, X-JIT-OTP, X-Request-ID,
+  Idempotency-Key` — the F-12 fix headers are landed there.
+- `gateway/service/app.py:271` (the **customer gateway** — the service that
+  mounts the `/api/v1/*` + `/v1/chat/completions` surfaces the Studio browser
+  actually calls) allow-list is the 9-header set: `Authorization,
+  Content-Type, X-SupremeAI-Key, X-Guest-Mode, X-Forwarded-For, Accept,
+  Origin, Referer, X-Correlation-ID` — **none of the bundle headers**.
+- The live 11-header list = the gateway 9-set + `Accept-Language,
+  Content-Language` (the deployed revision differs slightly from main, but
+  the four missing headers are absent in BOTH the repo list and the live
+  response — the invariant finding holds under either deploy skew).
+
+**Fixer routing correction**: patching `core/app_builder.py` cannot heal the
+customer surface — the preflight that kills the Studio bundle is answered by
+the gateway process. The one-line-class fix is extending
+`gateway/service/app.py:271`'s `allow_headers` with the Studio bundle's
+headers (`X-CSRF-Token, X-Conversation-Id, X-Device-Fingerprint, X-JIT-OTP,
+X-Request-ID, X-Trusted-Browser`), ideally sharing a single header-set
+constant with `core/app_builder.py:408` so the two surfaces cannot drift
+apart again — the exact private-duplicate drift class retired for the Tower
+URL resolvers in PR #2324 this same cycle.
+
